Over the weekend I saw a remarkable new printer by Canon.
It is called the BJC-5000.  Here is what is remarkable about it:

1. Support for 11x17" paper!
2. TWO LARGE ink cartriges.  And you can use different 
   cartriges depending on what you are printing!  Use
   a color/black cartridge + a large black cartridge for
   fast black and white printing and good color.  Use
   a color/black cartidge + a 4 color cartridge for
   7 color photo printing.  Use 2 black cartidges for FAST
   black and white printing, or two of the combined
   color/black cartridges!
3. 1440x720 dpi resolution
4. Its price.  At Staples, $250!!!

Has anyone ever used this printer with Windows NT 4.0?
Has anyone ever used this printer with Alpha NT?

With the rash of printers coming out that rely on the
CPU to do its thinking, I am getting weary about
buying these low-price printers with high-end features
and quality.

Thanks!
