Not that specific printer, but I have used the 4300, it's sibling.  Alpha 
drivers for the entire Canon series are on Microsoft's WHQL site 
(http://www.microsoft.com/hwtest/) -- the 5000 uses the same driver as the 
4000 series.  That's one of the nice things about Canon printers, they 
don't use Highly Proprietary (snicker) drivers for each variant of each 
printer -- one driver fits all with Canon.

I'm just about to purchase a refurb Canon MultiPASS C5000 -- it uses the 
same drivers and print accessories as the one you referenced, but also has 
stand-alone FAX and color copy capabilities!  I've found it through 
www.pricewatch.com for $249 (with a 1 year warranty from Canon)!  (I don't 
mind refurb -- with the volume that I do at home, it's adequate for me; I 
publish all my important stuff on the Internet!)

