You do not have to use IPX.  You can use one or all or a combination of
protocols with Jetadmin.  The printer does not have to be on the same subnet
to print to it, though it does have to be on it for configuration/initial
setup (if using an external jetdirect).  Using the computer version of
Jetadmin (WebJetAdmin does allow for config across subnets).  I've used the
latest version of Jetadmin on the Alpha with HPLJ4k's, HPLJ5 and HPLJ5M's so
I dont see why you'd have a problem with a 5k.  I'd think you would have a
harder time finding a native version of the print driver (as said below)
than you would setting up Jetadmin on your box.

