From mark.herdeg@digital.com Fri, 13 Nov 1998 13:49:25 -0500
Message-ID: <3FE0A842BADBD111A9E70000F8083C341895A5@lkgexc3.bb.dec.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 1998 13:49:25 -0500
From: Mark Herdeg <mark.herdeg@digital.com>
Subject: RE: Real Player G2 better...but no video.
To: "'AlphaNT Mail List'" <AlphaNT@alphant.com>
Reply-To: AlphaNT Mail List <AlphaNT@AlphaNT.com>

On yet another note, programs like realplayer, and even netscape and such do
those "smart update" type things where they download new parts and put them
in
on top of themselves..so far FX seems to deal with this alright but I wonder
if
it's causing some confusion because it thinks it's the same executable? I've
gotten in the habit with smaller programs of just renaming the newer exe or 
taking out the older version's profile..but that's just a concern, anyway..

You don't have to worry about this. FX!32 determines whether 2 executables
or DLLs are the same by doing essentially a whole-file checksum on them, not
by seeing if they have the same name. That means that you can rename an EXE
and FX!32 won't care. Likewise, you can replace an EXE with a new version
that has the same name, and FX!32 will know it has to start a fresh profile
and optimization. In the latter case, it will also automatically detect that
it can delete the profile and optimization for the overwritten file.

Mark Herdeg

