David,

I don't want to spoil your excitement, but cable modem, similarly to
frame-relay use a "shared cloud" for the whole neighborhood or even town. So
yes, the speed rules today, because it's new and you are one of the first
people on . . . . But in a year or two when cable modem popularity  picks up
(which it surely will) you'll have to share your bandwidth with your
neighbors. If available in you neighborhood, xDSL would be a much better
choice since you have a true point-to-point line to your provider . . . .

Peter

